Or no, that was Michael.
或者不对，那是迈克尔。

1481
00:54:54.560 --> 00:54:55.960
When Michael was like, how old are you?
当迈克尔问“你多大了”的时候。

1482
00:54:56.000 --> 00:55:00.680
But anyway, we learned that Creed was in an iron lung as a teenager, which is hilarious.
但总之，我们了解到克里德十几岁时住过铁肺，这太搞笑了。

1483
00:55:01.640 --> 00:55:06.480
I love in this episode that Michael takes off his microphone.
我喜欢这一集里迈克尔摘下麦克风的桥段。

1484
00:55:06.740 --> 00:55:07.100
Yes.
没错。

1485
00:55:07.280 --> 00:55:09.440
This is the first time we go radio silent, right?
这是我们第一次进入无线电静默状态，对吧？

1486
00:55:09.440 --> 00:55:10.000
I think so.
我想是的。

1487
00:55:10.000 --> 00:55:12.120
That we point out that we're actually miked.
我们第一次指出我们其实戴着麦克风。

1488
00:55:12.300 --> 00:55:12.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1489
00:55:12.350 --> 00:55:14.020
We sort of break that fourth wall in that way.
我们以那种方式打破了第四面墙。

1490
00:55:14.140 --> 00:55:14.320
Yeah.
是啊。

1491
00:55:14.820 --> 00:55:15.900
I liked that.
我喜欢那样。

1492
00:55:16.140 --> 00:55:18.640
And then I love this scene.
然后我喜欢这一幕。

1493
00:55:18.640 --> 00:55:20.900
And this scene was not in the script.
这一幕不在剧本里。

1494
00:55:21.220 --> 00:55:24.460
In our shooting draft of the script, they must have added this later.
在我们拍摄用的剧本草稿里，他们一定是后来加进去的。

1495
00:55:24.460 --> 00:55:31.840
I mean, probably while we were shooting, but this scene where Jim calls Pam and Angela pops
我是说，可能是在我们拍摄的时候，但这一幕是吉姆给帕姆打电话，安吉拉

1496
00:55:31.840 --> 00:55:37.160
her head over to overhear if there's any news about Dwight and Pam clocks it.
探过头来想听听有没有关于德怀特的消息，而帕姆注意到了。

1497
00:55:37.840 --> 00:55:47.060
And then Pam goes over to Oscar and tells Oscar, hey, Oscar, I thought you'd like to know Dwight's going to be okay.
然后帕姆走到奥斯卡身边告诉他，嘿，奥斯卡，我想你应该想知道德怀特会没事的。

1498
00:55:47.480 --> 00:55:50.080
And it zooms in on your face.
然后镜头拉近到你的脸上。

1499
00:55:50.800 --> 00:55:52.180
And you're so relieved.
你看起来如释重负。

1500
00:55:52.400 --> 00:55:56.160
And you can tell you're in love.
你能看出来你坠入爱河了。

1501
00:55:56.340 --> 00:55:56.960
I'm in love.
我恋爱了。

1502
00:55:57.000 --> 00:55:58.120
I was worried about my man.
我当时很担心我的男人。

1503
00:55:58.300 --> 00:56:02.860
One of the things I did, and we all did this in different ways as characters.
我做过的一件事，其实我们每个人都以不同的方式作为角色做过这件事。

1504
00:56:03.420 --> 00:56:12.100
If something interesting was happening at reception, even if it wasn't in my script that my character clocked it, I would just pop up and look over the partition.
如果接待处发生了什么有趣的事，即使剧本里没写我的角色注意到了，我也会探出头去看看隔板那边。

1505
00:56:12.600 --> 00:56:19.380
And the first time one of the camera guys caught me doing it, the writers loved this, and that kind of became a thing.
第一次被摄影师抓到我这么做时，编剧们很喜欢，后来这就成了我的一个标志性动作。

1506
00:56:19.660 --> 00:56:24.920
So, of course, if Pam is on the phone about Dwight, I'm going to pop my head over.
所以，当然了，如果帕姆在电话里谈论德怀特，我肯定会探头过去听。

1507
00:56:25.100 --> 00:56:29.020
But this one was scripted, that my head's there, that I'm listening in.
但这一幕是写在剧本里的，写着我的头在那儿，我在偷听。

1508
00:56:29.400 --> 00:56:34.820
And I remember one of the things they told me is that they're going to catch my head at the top.
我记得他们告诉过我，他们会拍到我探出的头。

1509
00:56:35.240 --> 00:56:36.400
It's not a ton of time.
时间并不长。

1510
00:56:36.400 --> 00:56:39.040
Pam's going to look back over, and then I need to, like, disappear.
帕姆回头看的时候，我就得赶紧消失。

1511
00:56:41.200 --> 00:56:43.920
And so we were playing around with this.
所以我们当时在尝试各种演法。

1512
00:56:43.980 --> 00:56:46.940
So in one take, when you look back over, I just dropped to my knees.
在其中一条拍摄中，当你回头看时，我直接跪在了地上。

1513
00:56:47.280 --> 00:56:48.760
Do you notice how quickly?
你注意到有多快了吗？

1514
00:56:48.900 --> 00:56:49.560
You really do.
你真的注意到了。

1515
00:56:49.800 --> 00:56:53.540
And that's the one I think they kept in because I just, like, dropped like a rock.
我想他们保留的就是那一条，因为我当时就像石头一样直接坠下去了。

1516
00:56:53.680 --> 00:56:55.160
And they thought that was really funny.
他们觉得那特别好笑。

1517
00:56:55.380 --> 00:57:06.580
The very end of this, it's the final shot of Dwight in the CT scan machine, and Michael tries to put his foot in.
这一集的最后，是德怀特在CT扫描机里的最后一个镜头，迈克尔试图把脚伸进去。

1518
00:57:07.140 --> 00:57:08.360
That was not in the script.
那不在剧本里。

1519
00:57:08.360 --> 00:57:11.380
That was an improvisation by Mr. Steve Carell.
那是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔先生的即兴发挥。

1520
00:57:11.460 --> 00:57:12.140
Of course.
当然了。

1521
00:57:12.340 --> 00:57:12.900
Of course.
当然了。

1522
00:57:13.120 --> 00:57:17.560
So we learn in this episode that Dwight with a concussion is actually really a likable guy.
所以我们在这一集里了解到，脑震荡后的德怀特其实是个挺讨人喜欢的人。

1523
00:57:17.720 --> 00:57:17.960
Yeah.
没错。

1524
00:57:18.100 --> 00:57:20.400
But he also steps out of his lane a little.
但他也有点越界了。

1525
00:57:20.580 --> 00:57:21.920
With Pam, he becomes a friend.
他和帕姆成了朋友。

1526
00:57:22.040 --> 00:57:22.820
Jim didn't like that.
吉姆不喜欢那样。

1527
00:57:23.160 --> 00:57:26.880
And then he gets the jokes instead of Michael with the doctor.
而且在医生面前，他抢了迈克尔的梗。

1528
00:57:27.080 --> 00:57:28.300
And Michael didn't like that.
迈克尔也不喜欢那样。

1529
00:57:28.940 --> 00:57:30.400
And, you know, I don't know.
而且，你知道，我不知道该怎么说。

1530
00:57:30.520 --> 00:57:32.920
I thought he was so adorable in this episode.
我觉得他在这一集里太可爱了。

1531
00:57:32.920 --> 00:57:40.940
Well, a lot of people pointed out that there are going to be some future episodes that follow the Pam and Dwight friendship.
嗯，很多人指出，未来的剧集里会有一些关于帕姆和德怀特友谊的情节。

1532
00:57:41.240 --> 00:57:47.440
And spoiler alert, in the end, Dwight calls Pam one of his best friends or his best friend.
剧透预警，最后德怀特称帕姆为他最好的朋友之一，或者就是他最好的朋友。

1533
00:57:47.440 --> 00:57:48.080
I know.
我知道。

1534
00:57:48.440 --> 00:57:49.520
And it's really sweet.
真的很暖心。

1535
00:57:49.520 --> 00:57:52.240
And I absolutely loved these.
我非常喜欢这些情节。

1536
00:57:52.500 --> 00:57:55.920
I love whenever Pam and Dwight have to team up.
我喜欢帕姆和德怀特联手的任何时候。

1537
00:57:56.060 --> 00:58:03.520
I think something about Pam that's true is that for as much as Dwight and or Michael annoy her, she really loves them.
我觉得帕姆身上有一点是真实的，那就是尽管德怀特或者迈克尔让她很烦，但她其实真的很爱他们。

1538
00:58:03.780 --> 00:58:04.860
Like, she does.
真的，她是这样。

1539
00:58:05.100 --> 00:58:08.980
They're her crazy cousin or zany uncle or whatever.
他们就像是她的疯狂表亲或古怪叔叔之类的。

1540
00:58:09.940 --> 00:58:11.180
But she loves them.
但她爱他们。

1541
00:58:11.420 --> 00:58:12.440
She does love them.
她是真的爱他们。

1542
00:58:12.780 --> 00:58:15.000
I have to think that Angela does not.
我不得不认为安吉拉可不这么想。

1543
00:58:15.800 --> 00:58:18.040
If Angela doesn't like you, she doesn't like you.
如果安吉拉不喜欢你，她是真的不喜欢你。

1544
00:58:18.080 --> 00:58:18.900
She doesn't like you.
她就是不喜欢你。

1545
00:58:18.980 --> 00:58:25.260
And I have to think that it was probably like a source of conflict for her and Dwight if Dwight was like, well, you know, Pam was kind of – I'm like, oh, Pam.
我不得不认为，如果德怀特说“嗯，你知道，帕姆其实挺……”的时候，这可能会成为她和德怀特之间的冲突来源，我当时就想，噢，帕姆。

1546
00:58:25.640 --> 00:58:30.940
You know, I'm going to say I think the one person that Pam maybe didn't like was Angela.
你知道，我想说，我觉得帕姆唯一可能不喜欢的人就是安吉拉。

1547
00:58:31.180 --> 00:58:31.700
I know.
我知道。

1548
00:58:32.660 --> 00:58:33.660
Like, I think.
我是这么觉得的。

1549
00:58:33.720 --> 00:58:34.100
I know.
我知道。

1550
00:58:34.100 --> 00:58:40.360
She – you know, but she'll take the if you have nothing good to say, say nothing at all about Angela.
她——你知道，但对于安吉拉，她会遵循“如果你说不出什么好话，就什么也别说”的原则。

1551
00:58:40.820 --> 00:58:42.880
Yeah, but I really don't think they liked each other.
是啊，但我真的觉得他们互相看不顺眼。

1552
00:58:42.880 --> 00:58:43.920
I don't think they did.
我也觉得。

1553
00:58:44.040 --> 00:58:44.760
Which is hilarious.
这太搞笑了。

1554
00:58:44.980 --> 00:58:53.160
If you have the DVDs and want to watch a really great deleted scene from this episode, my personal favorite is the scene where Jim and Michael,
如果你有DVD，想看这一集里一个非常棒的删减片段，我个人最喜欢的是吉姆和迈克尔的那一段，

1555
00:58:53.160 --> 00:58:56.280
they are in the waiting room of the emergency room.
他们在急诊室的候诊室里。

1556
00:58:56.480 --> 00:58:56.800
Oh.
噢。

1557
00:58:57.020 --> 00:58:57.940
Dwight is in the back.
德怀特在后面。

1558
00:58:58.080 --> 00:58:59.360
They're waiting in this lobby.
他们在大厅里等着。

1559
00:58:59.660 --> 00:59:00.440
I watched this.
我看过这个。

1560
00:59:00.460 --> 00:59:02.140
They're watching a telenovela.
他们在看一部肥皂剧。

1561
00:59:02.860 --> 00:59:04.760
And it just made me laugh.
这真的把我逗乐了。

1562
00:59:05.020 --> 00:59:09.500
They're just stuck in this hospital waiting room watching a telenovela, and I loved it.
他们被困在医院的候诊室里看肥皂剧，我太喜欢这一幕了。

1563
00:59:09.760 --> 00:59:11.500
Well, guys, that's the injury.
好吧，伙计们，这就是那个伤口。

1564
00:59:11.820 --> 00:59:12.720
That's the injury.
就是那个伤口。

1565
